" hi's vim override, kept to the minimum that earns the `-u`: vim's own shipped
" defaults, so the alias is not a downgrade, plus the OSC 52 yank autocmd,
" which is hi's and has no other home. Nothing to taste lives here - your own
" $_HI_CONFIG_DIR/vim.rc replaces this file wholesale.

" must be first: `vim -u <file>` implies 'compatible', which disables <> key
" notation and a good deal else. defaults.vim clears it too, but that file is
" not on every vim and never on neovim.
set nocompatible

" the out-of-the-box editor rather than the 1976 one, spelled the way vim
" itself spells it. `unlet!` because a system vimrc may have set the skip flag;
" `silent!` because neovim ships no such file and needs none.
unlet! skip_defaults_vim
silent! source $VIMRUNTIME/defaults.vim

" belt and braces for a vim old enough to have no defaults.vim; neovim has both
" on already, and setting them twice costs nothing.
syntax enable
filetype plugin indent on

" Yank -> the client's clipboard; common/osc52.sh does the encoding/wrapping,
" this only decides *when*. Four honest conditions: the toggle, the event
" (exists('##...') - neovim lies to has('patch-')), $_HI_OSC52 (empty outside
" a session), and the unnamed register - "ay stays local, a delete a delete.
if $_HI_DISABLE_OSC52 != '1' && exists('##TextYankPost') && filereadable($_HI_OSC52)
  augroup hi_osc52
    autocmd!
    autocmd TextYankPost *
          \ if v:event.operator ==# 'y' && v:event.regname ==# '' |
          \   silent call system('sh ' . shellescape($_HI_OSC52),
          \                      join(v:event.regcontents, "\n")) |
          \ endif
  augroup END
endif
